# Optional. While you run `npx expo start`, the app finds your computer by
# itself and calls Django on port 8000 there:
#   Android emulator                    -> http://10.0.2.2:8000
#   phone with Expo Go on the same Wi-Fi -> http://<your computer's Wi-Fi IP>:8000
# The terminal running Expo prints the address in use, as "[api] Using API server ...".
#
# Copy this file to .env (in this frontend folder) only to use a different
# server, remove the # from one line below, then restart `npx expo start -c`.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://13.246.11.197
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8000
